SRC/eff_tsmon -- changes made for the OSK freeware collection  tsmon2.c  When the line would not open it printed                tsmon2: Can't open device "/t9" -            and exited with the error code, leaving Microware's shell to            print the reason after the dash.  Any other shell printed            nothing there.  It now prints the reason itself with prerr(),            as its own `can't fork' message already did.  Rebuilt -qm,            2026-09-26.  The original is tsmon2.c.ori.